  "body": "Wanted: the Tormach mill post (`tormach.cps`) writes three things that PathPilot supports. Today the post or the engine refuses each one by name:\n- work offsets 10-500 (`G54.1 P<n>`);\n- a reverse spindle (`M4`) and left-hand tapping (`G74`);\n- control cutter compensation (`G41`/`G42` with `D`, `G41.1`/`G42.1`).\n\nEvidence (upstream/main `1c0152c91`):\n- `assets/posts/tormach.cps:26`: `workOffsetMax = 9`; `:476` refuses higher offsets.\n- `tormach.cps:620`: the spindle start is always `M3`.\n- `tormach.cps:1313-1326`: the tap cycle is always `G84`.\n- `crates/post/src/post/engine.rs:308-313`: the engine refuses a reverse mill spindle because the post does not declare `millSpindleReverse`.\n- `tormach.cps:464`: `onRadiusCompensation` refuses.\n- Tormach PathPilot mill operator's manual UM10587, the G-code chapter (pp. 207-208, 217-219, 228).\n- #3409 covers `G54.1 P` only for `tormach-mill-turn-spindle.cps`.\n\nFound by the post audit against the Tormach manuals (#4130).\n\nDone means:\n- Offsets 10-500 post as `G54.1 P<n>`, and a golden test pins one.\n- The post declares `millSpindleReverse`. A left-hand cut posts `M4`, and a left-hand tap posts `G74`. A test pins each one.\n- Control compensation posts `G41`/`G42` with a `D` word, or the reason for the refusal is recorded in `docs/decisions/`.\n- A right-hand program posts the same output as before.\n",
